  "extraction_notes": "Page 6 is the bound-in 'alterations since dissolution/date of election' notice (C5), signed 4/07/2019, the same date used for statement_date. Page 7 is a separate, later single-page alteration notice (received 29/07/2019), distinct from page 6's bound-in notice, despite the similar heading. Page 9 is only the signature/date continuation of page 8's notice (signed 29/06/2020); it carries no items of its own but is included in pages_covered. Section 9's spouse cell 'Motor vehicle, self-managed superannuation fund, UK NHS Pension, life insurance policy' and section 12's 'Qantas and Virgin Australia' cells (self and spouse, pages 4 and 8) were split one item per asset/provider per C6, medium confidence. Page 8's section 14 rows describe the member's fiancee becoming his spouse/partner and a correction to the niece's employer (Australian Airports Association -> Australasian Railway Association); recorded as removed/varied pairs per C7, medium confidence. Page 11's 'Joint tenant with spouse/partner' (real estate) and 'Joint home loan with spouse/partner' (Westpac) entries were treated per C1 as self+spouse items; the real-estate self item is 'varied' (paired with the page-11 deletion of the sole-ownership version from page 10) while the new joint home loan has no explicit deletion counterpart in the source and was recorded as 'added' for both owners, medium confidence, even though it may relate to the solely-held Westpac home loan declared on the initial statement. Page 13 is a handwritten notice correcting the spouse's home loan creditor from 'My State' to 'Westpac' (removed/varied pair), signed '11 Mar 21' (the member's other names also updated to 'Andrew Damien Wilkie' on this page, a form-field change only, not recorded as an item)."
